NOTE (why we’re backfilling):
- The MSNE runs already produced the needed perf metadata in meta/timev_msne.txt (Elapsed time + MaxRSS).
- Those lines are tab/whitespace-prefixed, so the existing R parser (anchored with ^Elapsed/^Maximum) fails to match and writes NA.
- Backfilling parses the existing timev_msne.txt correctly and updates the per-task + aggregate TSVs, avoiding an expensive HPC rerun.

The backfilling script is run from the root of this project like this:

# From repo root

# Feature perturbations (array_20323876)
python Scripts/method_comparisons/performance_jobs/MSNE/backfill_msne_time_mem.py \
  Results/Performance_benchmarks/Feature_perturbations/MSNE/array_20323876 \
  --no-bak

# Sample perturbations (array_20323877)
python Scripts/method_comparisons/performance_jobs/MSNE/backfill_msne_time_mem.py \
  Results/Performance_benchmarks/Sample_perturbations/MSNE/array_20323877 \
  --no-bak
